#   938B6E15E0759D4FD8F5D47AE921550ADEB3E5B762A17A2D6497A97A8FCD7777.
# Probe: scripts/scratch/2026-10_c2_stress/quickjs_stress_live.py (one-off scratch; the
#   first run used its pre-rename remote name C:\temp\c2_stress_live.py, identical bytes).

## (1) The change

Four source/test edits, no build-system change:

    src/dll/quickjs/quickjs_wrapper.c     + c2_stress_script[] and int C2EvalStress(void)
    src/dll/exports.zig                   + extern fn C2EvalStress() c_int;
                                          + export fn C2EvalStressOne() = n*4+3 encoding
    src/dll/quickjs/c2_diag_test.zig      + native test calling C2EvalStress directly
    scripts/test_c2_harness.py            + "C2EvalStressOne" in the known-export tuple

`C2EvalStress` is a thin wrapper over the existing `C2EvalProbe`: one fixed script text,
one evaluation, the same `n*4+3` thread-exit-code encoding. The script lives once, in C;
the native test calls the same symbol instead of copying the text.

## (2) The script and the paths it drives

    (function(){
    var acc=0;
    for(var r=0;r<8;r++){
    var s='';
    for(var i=0;i<2000;i++)s+='abcdefgh'+i;
    acc=(acc+s.length)&0xffff;
    var a=[];
    for(var j=0;j<4000;j++)a.push({k:j,v:'v'+j});
    acc=(acc+a.length+a[3999].v.length)&0xffff;
    var t=JSON.stringify(a);
    acc=(acc+t.length)&0xffff;
    }
    return acc;
    })()

Vendored-QuickJS call sites behind each construct (quickjs.c):

    4146 / 4177   string builder growth      js_realloc2 -> js_realloc_rt
    9622          array growth               js_realloc2 -> js_realloc_rt
    1880          the realloc/usable path    js_malloc_usable_size_rt -> __js_malloc_usable_size
    various       per-round refcount drops   __js_free

The 8 fallback `container_of` expressions §48 removed instrumentation from are
quickjs.c:1494 (`js_rc`) plus 1601/1607 (`__js_free`), 1645/1651/1684 (`__js_realloc`)
and 1704/1711 (`__js_malloc_usable_size`). Only 1494 was on the §49 path. The arithmetic
uses only lengths, integer string digits and insertion-order JSON, so its result is a
deterministic int32; the expected value 15904 was computed independently with Node from
the same source text, and pinning it in the native test makes a divergence loud.

