## (6) Judgment

- The in-game result equals the independently computed expectation: `rc=63619` →
  n = (63619-3)/4 = 15904. A corrupted context, a short-circuit, or engine-divergent
  semantics (different number formatting or JSON key order) would have produced a
  different int32; none did.
- The churn is allocator-heavy: 8 rounds × (2000 string concatenations growing the
  builder, 4000 object pushes growing the array, `JSON.stringify` of a 4000-element
  array), with each round dropping its strings/array/JSON text. Every allocation, growth
  and free goes through our `heap_mf`/HeapAlloc. If any of the seven un-instrumented
  `container_of` sites still aborted, the remote thread would have died with status 3
  and the host would be gone — the §45/§49 signature. It is not.
- Two runs, two module copies, same artifact: the outcome does not depend on the
  allocator layout or ASLR base. §48's one-include repair now has live evidence on the
  exact seven sites it was meant to protect, not only on `js_rc`.

## (7) Boundaries

- Fixed script only. This is not a general evaluation API and does not lift the P21/C3
  boundary (caller-supplied JS text stays deferred).
- Main menu, no scene load, no mod script evaluation. QuickJS evaluates our script via
  the DLL's own `JS_Eval`; the engine's script parser is not involved. C3 (routing) and
  C4 (visible effect) are untouched.
- The script's constructs imply the realloc/usable-size/free paths by source reading;
  the run is not instrumented per call site, so it cannot claim each of the seven ran
  individually (e.g. an in-place grow that skips usable-size would not be counted). What
  it proves is that a large allocator churn on the repaired artifact does not abort.
- One game session and one artifact; two module copies. The known per-copy QuickJS
  runtime leak (reset without free) still applies and was not observable here.
- Fence lesson recorded: a new scratch probe named `c2_stress_live.py` violated R-depth
  (the `c2_*` prefix is reserved for the maintained top-level family and the `C:/temp`
  wire contract). It was renamed to `quickjs_stress_live.py`; the first shot used the old
  remote name with identical bytes.
- The game was left running; no detour was installed.

## (8) Read-only self-attestation

    - no hook/Interceptor/patchCode/writeByteArray/Memory.protect; no debugger attach;
      no game-file changes; no byte edits.
    - Windows host ran only scp/Get-FileHash and `python` probes.
    - the artifact was built locally by Zig and transferred without modification.

## (9) Counts for §50

1 game session (pid 9932, reused from §49, never restarted); 2 injected module copies
(one per run); 6 dispatches (2 × [C2Sanity, C2Init, C2EvalStressOne]); 0 hooks, 0 byte
